@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam ArrowColor #415A77
skinparam rectangleBorderColor #415A77
skinparam rectangleBackgroundColor #F4F7FA

title Collection traversal: one revision, two ownership products

rectangle "Live Rust dictionary\n(any applicable automaton)" as live #D9EAD3
rectangle "O(1) immutable\nsnapshot root / graph" as snap #D9EAD3
rectangle "Generic monomorphic\nentry traversal" as walk #B6D7A8
rectangle "Pure Rust\nIterator + fold/visitor" as rust #93C47D
rectangle "Optional batched ABI\nvt.dict.entry.v1" as abi #FCE5CD
rectangle "Host-owned immutable\nSet / Map / Iterable view" as materialized #CFE2F3
rectangle "Closeable streaming\ncursor / reducer" as stream #9FC5E8

live --> snap : capture once
snap --> walk : pins revision
walk --> rust : no FFI or vtable
walk --> abi : descriptors + unit arena
abi --> materialized : drain, validate, close\nbefore iterator escapes
abi --> stream : bounded lease\nlexical close

note bottom of snap
Concurrent mutation publishes another revision.
Existing iterators remain stable and hold no writer lock.
end note

note bottom of materialized
Ordinary early loop exit is leak-safe:
the native snapshot is already released.
end note

note bottom of stream
Large dictionaries avoid O(output) host memory;
try-with-resources / using / context manager.
end note
@enduml
